From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: knapcio <knapcio@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 21:16:50 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 14/31] S2: per-session MTP confidence stop in shared rounds
 behind G6_MTP_KSTOPB, shared-round log under G6_MTP_LPLOG

round_all verified the same k drafts for every session. With G6_MTP_KSTOPB=1 each session verifies its own k_q: the
most j with p_1 * .. * p_i >= t_i for every i <= j (the MTP head's merged log-probabilities, the same bytes on every
rank), at least G6_MTP_KSTOPB_KMIN (0|1). Thresholds G6_MTP_KSTOPB_TAU (default 0.6,0.88), or G6_MTP_KSTOPB_TAU_S<n>
for rounds of n sessions. The chain still drafts K, the main step keeps class row_class(K + 1). capture_all adds the
main widths the rule reaches (S..S*(K+1)); G6_MTP_KSTOPB_WIDTHS limits them, a round then fills up to a captured width
with the most likely unverified drafts. G6_MTP_KSTOPB_EXPLORE=n (measurement): every n-th round verifies hashed counts,
so one log times every width. The policy is in the S2 runtime signature. Off (default): the planner's steps are
unchanged (host trace identical to the previous header).

G6_MTP_LPLOG now also prints, per shared round, "# kstopb" (sessions, main width, per session verified/accepted/held
counts and the drafts' log-probabilities, a hash of the inputs) and "# kstopb_ms" (host ms of the round's main, draft
and chain steps). Host test batch_kstopb_test.
